        <mxCell id="note-notifications-audit-outbox" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-family:Arial;font-size:12px&quot;&gt;The SQL migration is canonical. PK/FK/UQ/IDX markers identify columns; CHECK constraints are listed on each table. FK column labels name the referenced table and key. All values are synthetic schema metadata.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Foreign keys to other pages:&lt;/b&gt; notifications.user_id → users.id; availability_subscriptions.customer_id → users.id; availability_subscriptions.product_id → products.id; availability_subscriptions.pharmacy_id → pharmacies.id; reminders.customer_id → users.id; reminders.product_id → products.id; notification_preferences.user_id → users.id; audit_entries.actor_id → users.id&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;schema_migrations&lt;/b&gt; is a technical migration ledger created by the runner, not a domain table.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;strokeColor=#8295A8;fillColor=#F2F6FA;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
